![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

The `network->libertyPort(pin)` call can return `nullptr` if the pin does not correspond to a valid liberty port. Accessing `port->name()` without a null check can lead to a null pointer dereference and crash. Please add a null check before accessing `port`.

```suggestion
      sta::LibertyPort* port = network->libertyPort(pin);
      if (port == nullptr) {
        continue;
      }
      std::string port_name = port->name();
