![critical](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/critical.svg)

The format string passed to `logger->error` contains two `{}` placeholders, but no corresponding arguments are provided. This will cause a runtime error or crash when this error path is triggered. Please pass `network->name(instance)` and `cell_name` as arguments.

```c
        logger->error(utl::CUT,
                      50,
                      "Instance {} of type {} has more than one output connected. "
                      "Multioutput cells with more than one output used are not supported.",
                      network->name(instance),
                      cell_name);
```

![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

The `sta::InstancePinIterator` returned by `network->pinIterator(instance)` is dynamically allocated on the heap and must be deleted to avoid a memory leak. Wrapping it in a `std::unique_ptr` is the idiomatic way to ensure it is safely deleted when it goes out of scope.

```c
    std::unique_ptr<sta::InstancePinIterator> pin_iter(
        network->pinIterator(instance));
```

![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

The `network->libertyPort(pin)` call can return `nullptr` if the pin does not correspond to a valid liberty port. Accessing `port->name()` without a null check can lead to a null pointer dereference and crash. Please add a null check before accessing `port`.

```suggestion
      sta::LibertyPort* port = network->libertyPort(pin);
      if (port == nullptr) {
        continue;
      }
      std::string port_name = port->name();
```

![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

`abc::SC_CellPinName(current_cell, i)` returns a raw `char*` pointer which could potentially be `nullptr`. Constructing a `std::string` implicitly from a null pointer causes undefined behavior and a crash. Please store the result in a temporary pointer and check for `nullptr` before inserting into the maps.

```c
      const char* pin_name = abc::SC_CellPinName(current_cell, i);
      if (pin_name != nullptr) {
        if (truth_table == constant_0) {
          const0_gates_.insert({current_cell->pName, pin_name});
        }

        if (truth_table == constant_1) {
          const1_gates_.insert({current_cell->pName, pin_name});
        }
      }
```

